    "shot": "shots/n011.jpg",
    "resolution": "Fixed with soft particles. The 'shadow' was the silhouette of the flat quad each beam is painted on — sliced along a straight line wherever it passed through the floor. The opaque scene now renders into a depth texture first and each beam fades as it approaches whatever is behind it, so it behaves like a volume instead of a sheet. Plus a near-fade for walking into a beam, and a wider facing fade for beams slicing open air.",
